The classifier scored 0/20 as harmful, yet at least 4 documents (records 4, 7, 8, 20) are clearly adult/NSFW — all false negatives on Chinese-language content. The classifier is trained on English text and is essentially blind to non-English harmful content; lower confidence scores (0.90–0.95) correlate loosely with borderline cases, but no threshold on this classifier would reliably catch non-English NSFW. A threshold around **0.95 for non-NSFW** (i.e., flag anything predicted non-NSFW with confidence < 0.95 for review) would surface the 4 false-negative cases here, but domain/URL-based filtering is likely more reliable than content scoring for non-English content.
